tent player to the ad. Measured on the iOS e2e fleet"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"(catalog-pip, SDK 0.50.0-beta.500): the window opened before the break and","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"closed at "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"adbreakbegin"},{"type":"text","text":", with the ad playing full-screen in the main"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"window instead of inside it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Such players expose their own picture-in-picture facility with the missing"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"piece — THEOplayer retains the window across source changes when the host"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"constructs it with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PiPConfiguration(retainPresentationModeOnSourceChange: true)"},{"type":"text","text":" — but only if the window is driven through THAT facility. This"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"protocol is how an adapter hands the SDK that steering wheel; the renderer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"prefers it over its own controller whenever the content adapter conforms."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All three members are called on the main thread (the renderer is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@MainActor"},{"type":"text","text":"); the change handler must likewise be invoked on the main"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"thread, for every transition — including viewer-driven ones (the system UI"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can dismiss the window at any time), which is the whole reason the handler"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exists: the break format follows what is actually on screen."}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documenta